\\nDesign and implement the\\nsolution within Roxy Data Center\\nConfigure all required\\nDevOps, DevSecOps, and automation features\\nIntegrate with existing\\nMOE systems (identity, infrastructure, monitoring)\\nProvide documentation,\\nknowledge transfer, and training\\nDeliver ongoing support\\nand maintenance services\\n4. Functional Requirements\\n4.1 Source Code Management (SCM)\\nThe solution shall provide:\\nDistributed version\\ncontrol repositories\\nBranching, merging, and\\npull/merge request workflows\\nRole-based access\\ncontrol for repositories\\nWeb-based repository\\nmanagement interface\\nFull audit trail of code\\nchanges\\n4.2 CI/CD Pipeline Management\\nThe solution shall support:\\nDeclarative pipeline\\ndefinitions (e.g., YAML-based)\\nAutomated build, test,\\nand deployment workflows\\nEvent-based triggers\\n(code commits, schedules, API calls)\\nParallel and scalable\\npipeline execution\\nArtifact generation and\\nretention\\n4.3 Project and Work Management\\nThe platform shall include:\\nIssue and ticket\\nmanagement system\\nAgile boards (Scrum and\\nKanban)\\nSprint and milestone\\ntracking\\nCollaboration features\\n(comments, mentions, notifications)\\n4.4 Package and Artifact Repository\\nThe solution shall provide:\\nSupport for multiple\\npackage formats (containers, binaries, libraries)\\nVersion-controlled\\nartifact storage\\nDependency caching and\\nproxy capabilities\\n4.5 User and Access Management\\nThe platform shall support:\\nRole-Based Access\\nControl (RBAC)\\nIntegration with\\nenterprise identity systems (LDAP / Active Directory)\\nMulti-project and\\nmulti-team isolation\\nComprehensive audit\\nlogging\\n5. Advanced DevOps Requirements\\n5.1 DevSecOps Capabilities\\nThe solution shall include:\\nStatic code security\\nanalysis\\nDynamic application\\nsecurity testing\\nOpen-source dependency\\nvulnerability scanning\\nSecret detection\\nm echanisms\\nContainer security\\nscanning\\n5.2 Infrastructure as Code (IaC)\\nThe solution shall:\\nSupport infrastructure\\nprovisioning through code\\nEnable version control\\nof infrastructure definitions\\nIntegrate IaC into CI/CD\\npipelines\\n5.3 Deployment and Environment Management\\nThe platform shall provide:\\nMulti-environment\\nlifecycle management (Dev, Test, UAT, Production)\\nDeployment strategies\\nincluding:\\nBlue/Green\\nCanary\\nRolling deployments\\nEnvironment-specific\\nconfiguration control\\n5.4 Monitoring and Observability\\nThe solution shall support:\\nPipeline monitoring and\\nexecution tracking\\nIntegration with logging\\nand monitoring systems\\nAlerting and\\nnotification mechanisms\\nOperational dashboards\\n5.5 API and Integration\\nThe platform shall include:\\nComprehensive REST APIs\\nWebhook support for\\nintegrations\\nCompatibility with\\nthird-party tools and cloud services\\n6. Enterprise Requirements\\n6.1 Governance and Compliance\\nThe solution shall provide:\\nPolicy enforcement for\\npipelines and deployments\\nApproval workflows and\\nrelease gates\\nCompliance reporting and\\naudit trails\\n6.2 Analytics and Reporting\\nThe platform shall include:\\nDevOps performance\\nmetrics (e.g., deployment frequency, lead time)\\nPipeline efficiency\\nanalytics\\nTeam productivity\\ninsights\\n6.3 High Availability and Scalability\\nThe solution shall:\\nSupport clustered\\ndeployment architecture\\nEnable horizontal\\nscaling of workloads\\nProvide load balancing\\nand failover mechanisms\\n6.4 Backup and Disaster Recovery\\nThe platform shall include:\\nAutomated backup\\ncapabilities\\nPoint-in-time recovery\\nDisaster recovery\\noptions across sites\\n6.5 AI-Driven Capabilities (Optional)\\nVendors are encouraged to provide:\\nAI-assisted code\\nanalysis and recommendations\\nPredictive pipeline\\nfailure detection\\nIntelligent automation\\nand optimization features\\n7. Deployment Requirements\\nThe solution must be\\ndeployed on-premises at Roxy Data Center\\nSupport for private\\ncloud or hybrid architecture is preferred\\nMust align with MOE\\ninfrastructure standards (compute, storage, network)\\n8. Security Requirements\\nThe solution must:\\nEnsure encryption of\\ndata in transit and at rest\\nSupport Single Sign-On\\n(SSO), OAuth, and SAML\\nProvide fine-grained\\naccess controls\\nMaintain detailed audit logs for all activities\\n9. Operational Requirements\\nWeb-based user interface\\nCLI and API access\\nAutomated patching and\\nupgrade mechanisms\\nRole-based dashboards\\nand views\\n10. Licensing Requirements\\nVendors must provide:\\nFlexible licensing model\\nbased on:\\nNumber of users\\nCompute/pipeline\\ncapacity\\nStorage usage\\nTiered licensing options\\n(Core / Advanced / Enterprise)\\nClear definition of\\nincluded features per tier\\n11. Deliverables\\nThe vendor shall deliver:\\nFully deployed DevOps\\nplatform at Roxy Data Center\\nSoftware licenses and\\nactivation\\nConfiguration and\\nintegration with MOE systems\\nTechnical documentation\\nTraining sessions for\\nMOE teams\\nSupport and maintenance\\nservices""\n# Create PDF\npdf = FPDF()\npdf.add_page()\npdf.set_font("Arial", \'B\', 16)\npdf.cell(0,10,"Proposal Response", ln=True)\n\npdf.set_font("Arial", \'\', 12)\nfor line in rpf_text.split(\'\\n\'):\n    pdf.multi_cell(0,6,line)\n\n# Output PDF\npdf.output(str(pdf_path))\nprint(f"PDF written to {pdf_path}")\n'}
